Subject: Wifi: report authoritative local-MP disconnect transitions

ndsrecomp modification to vendored melonDS src/Wifi.cpp (GPLv3 5(a)
notice; see patches/README.md for the convention).

Calls the runner-owned nds_wifi_on_local_mp_disconnected hook whenever the
guest local-wireless state machine leaves MP mode: reset, client deauth, host
loss, received deauth, and host beacon-slot disable. A validated received UDP
datagram is evidence that a peer exists; these guest state-machine transitions
are the corresponding evidence that the session ended. This avoids keeping
save states disabled until radio power-off after a clean multiplayer exit.

--- a/src/Wifi.cpp
+++ b/src/Wifi.cpp
@@ (runner hook declarations)
+void nds_wifi_on_local_mp_disconnected();
@@ (each IsMP = false transition)
+    ::nds_wifi_on_local_mp_disconnected();
